  "final_message": "I fixed the bug. In `apply_discounts` in `billing/invoices.py`, the guard on line 131 used `and` where it needed `or`:\n\n```python\nif coupon is None and not applies_this_period(...)\n```\n\nWith `and`, a \"once\" coupon that had already been used still got applied to later invoices. The guard now reads `coupon is None or not applies_this_period(...)`, so it returns early in both cases.\n\nThe 24 existing tests pass. I didn't add your reproduction test to the suite, so I haven't run it. I also wrote `answer.json` with `{\"file\": \"invoices.py\", \"function\": \"apply_discounts\"}`.",
